### Changed

- Add the complete M9 Frontend Redesign milestone and its v1.9.0 release notes to `main` as one coherent release point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown answers, keeping citations without a title match in the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Add a primary ticket-header control that executes the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` item, with remaining suggestions available from an overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable command palette to every page, opened with `Ctrl/Cmd+K`, for navigation and ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Add optimistic status updates to the board and ticket detail view, reconciling successful changes with server state and restoring the prior state when a change is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Remove `AssignTicketDialog.razor` and `ChangeStatusDialog.razor` in favor of header-anchored menus for status and assignee changes. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges where citation titles appear in assistant answers, with hover and focus previews and a numbered sources fallback. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt so the assistant can use valid names for ticket assignments. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Add `tool_choice` enforcement that requires `check_grounding` once after retrieval when no check has run, before answer streaming. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Add shared design tokens for the palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors, and use the same constants to build `MudTheme`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Fix board-card title clamping by wrapping the title link so the two-line ellipsis can apply. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant panel's scoped selector so its padding and flex layout apply to `.assistant-chat`, keeping the send button inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Fix the ticket queue's Category column width and header styling so it stays aligned with Due without overlap. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add a chat system-prompt policy that requires successful tool results before claiming a change and avoids re-confirming changes the user already requested. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Fix ticket-summary timestamps by converting them to `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before adding them to the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Fix `search_knowledge_base` so non-transient failures return an error result while the unavailable path remains a non-error result. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Add semantic grounding scores based on sentence-to-passage embedding similarity, retaining lexical scoring as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
